Framework Computer's work
-------------------------
keyboards/framework/macropad/ is Framework's keyboard definition, taken from
https://github.com/FrameworkComputer/qmk_firmware, branch fl16-2025.
Copyright (C) 2022 Framework Computer.
Licensed GPL-2.0-or-later.

keymaps/palette/keymap.c is Framework's default macropad keymap with the layer
hooks removed. The keycode tables are theirs; the removal is mine.

keymap-dumps/framework-default.hex is a copy of the keymap Framework's compiled
layout produces in the module's EEPROM, so it is their layout too.
keymap-dumps/eeprom-keymap-2026-09-16.hex is the keymap this module was running
during the work, which is a remap of that layout.

The firmware image firmware-panel-palette.uf2 is built from that tree with these
files dropped in. It therefore contains Framework's and QMK's code, not only
mine. SOURCE.md records the exact commit, the submodule versions and the one
patch applied to the tree, and carries a written offer for the source.

QMK
---
QMK is at https://github.com/qmk/qmk_firmware, licensed GPL-2.0-or-later.

Other code in the image
-----------------------
QMK's RP2040 build links code from other projects, and the image therefore
contains it too:

* ChibiOS, licensed GPL-3.0, at https://www.chibios.org;
* the Raspberry Pi Pico SDK, licensed BSD-3-Clause, at
  https://github.com/raspberrypi/pico-sdk;
* small MIT and BSD licensed libraries that QMK vendors.

Their licence texts are in the build tree, under `lib/`. There is no separate
archive of them in this repository; SOURCE.md says how to get the tree and
carries a written offer for the complete source of the image.

VIA
---
VIA is the keyboard configurator at https://www.caniusevia.com. This repository
implements part of its raw HID protocol. VIA itself is not included.

